\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {39}{\ignorespaces What each experiment establishes---and the nearest conclusion it does \emph  {not} support. Four results are load-bearing---EXP-R1, the pre-registered EXP-R1b/R1c replication (both §\ref {sec:r1_faithful}), the parameter-free rule (§\ref {sec:hedging_baseline}) and the criterion-4 audit (§\ref {sec:external_audit}); EXP-A (§\ref {sec:prompt_equalized}) is \emph  {supporting}, showing the collapse is not one implementation, the factorial is a diagnostic, and transfer and human validation are in §\ref {sec:discussion}. Results are given in the text. \emph  {Unattributable} means the design cannot assign an effect to deception rather than to compliance with the instruction that produced it (§\ref {sec:identification}).}}{45}{table.caption.164}\protected@file@percent }
